---
# Pins the checks/behavior clang-tidy uses without this file so the CI job
# stays stable across clang-tidy versions instead of drifting with whatever
# a given version's defaults happen to be.
Checks: 'clang-diagnostic-*,clang-analyzer-*,-clang-analyzer-optin.cplusplus.UninitializedObject'
# UninitializedObject fires throughout this codebase for small value/handle
# types that deliberately leave POD members uninitialized at declaration and
# set them from the constructor body or an initializer that immediately
# follows construction - the same pattern already reviewed and suppressed
# for cppcheck's equivalent uninitMemberVar/uninitMemberVarNoCtor checks
# (see .cppcheck-suppressions).
# Only report findings located under our own src/ tree - vendored headers
# under third_party/ (SimpleIni, quickjs, delta, ...) are not ours to fix.
# Note this only filters clang-tidy's own checks (clang-analyzer-*); plain
# compiler diagnostics (clang-diagnostic-*) ignore this and are filtered by
# run-clang-tidy's file-name regex argument instead (see CMakeLists.txt).
HeaderFilterRegex: '.*/src/.*'
FormatStyle: none
